        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximate value function as",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        93.19036865234375,
        435.0758056640625,
        102.09693145751953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∆ˆV (xt, ut) = βE",
      "bbox": [
        316.958984375,
        108.32496643066406,
        390.98345947265625,
        120.60493469238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0002",
      "bbox": [
        392.636962890625,
        109.28948211669922,
        396.7913818359375,
        115.6655502319336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "V ϕψ(xt+1) | xt, ut",
      "bbox": [
        396.7879638671875,
        108.80416107177734,
        476.22064208984375,
        120.60493469238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0003",
      "bbox": [
        476.7149353027344,
        109.28948211669922,
        480.8693542480469,
        115.6655502319336
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "−E[V ϕψ(xt)]. (50)",
      "bbox": [
        480.97393798828125,
        108.80416107177734,
        563.0416870117188,
        120.60493469238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For a given xt and ut, there is a gap between the change",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399719238281,
        128.6559600830078,
        563.04052734375,
        139.2159423828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in the approximate and optimal value functions",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        140.6513671875,
        505.8699645996094,
        149.55792236328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "eV (xt, ut) = ∆ˆV (xt, ut) −∆V (xt, ut).",
      "bbox": [
        353.8809814453125,
        155.7859649658203,
        521.135986328125,
        168.644775390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(51)",
      "bbox": [
        546.4409790039062,
        158.46337890625,
        563.0387573242188,
        167.36993408203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To guarantee that the optimal value function, V (xt) actually",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        176.11598205566406,
        563.0376586914062,
        185.87794494628906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "decreases, the expected change in the approximate value",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        188.11138916015625,
        563.0354614257812,
        197.0179443359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "function must decrease by more than this gap,",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        199.9473876953125,
        502.0742492675781,
        208.85394287109375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∆ˆV (xt, ut) < eV (xt, ut).",
      "bbox": [
        383.9349670410156,
        215.0819854736328,
        491.08197021484375,
        227.9407958984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(52)",
      "bbox": [
        546.4441528320312,
        217.7593994140625,
        563.0419311523438,
        226.66595458984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Given that V (xt) is unknown in practice, this gap is also un-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        235.41200256347656,
        563.0401000976562,
        245.17396545410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "known. Thus, we simply aim to ensure that ∆ˆV (xt, ut) < 0.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        244.8219757080078,
        562.718505859375,
        257.1009521484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D. Simulation Experiment",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        269.44305419921875,
        419.2351989746094,
        278.03082275390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We explore this analysis empirically using a stochastic",
      "bbox": [
        321.93994140625,
        284.327392578125,
        563.0347290039062,
        293.23394775390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dubins Car dynamical system. The state is given as xt =",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779357910156,
        296.00299072265625,
        563.037841796875,
        306.3447570800781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "[rx ry θ]T where rx, ry denote the position and θ is the",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        304.3833923339844,
        563.033447265625,
        318.3999328613281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "orientation. The input is given as ut = [v ˙θ]T where v is the",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        316.5163879394531,
        563.0384521484375,
        330.3137512207031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "speed and ˙θ is the angular velocity. The nominal continuous",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        329.1789855957031,
        563.0285034179688,
        340.8739318847656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics are given as f(xt, ut) = [v cos(θ), v sin(θ), ˙θ]T .",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        340.1873779296875,
        563.0365600585938,
        353.4049072265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The stochastic, discrete-time dynamics applies Euler integra-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        355.63836669921875,
        563.0355834960938,
        364.544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion with ∆t = 0.1 sec and Gaussian process noise with",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        367.3149719238281,
        563.0353393554688,
        376.38092041015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Σf = [0.01 0.01 0.01]T .",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        375.6943664550781,
        413.10955810546875,
        389.4917297363281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We constructed a simple environment in which the goal is",
      "bbox": [
        321.93988037109375,
        391.1453552246094,
        563.0347900390625,
        400.0519104003906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "surrounded by dense obstacles arranged on a hexagonal lattice",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        402.9813537597656,
        563.035400390625,
        411.8879089355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(Fig. 17). Initial states are sampled at positions 7.5m away",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        414.657958984375,
        563.0352783203125,
        423.7239074707031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "from the goal with the orientation pointing towards the goal.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        426.65234375,
        561.3416137695312,
        435.55889892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We trained 13 actor-critic networks with increasingly large",
      "bbox": [
        321.93988037109375,
        438.48834228515625,
        563.0347290039062,
        447.3948974609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constraint penalties, γc. The inputs into these networks were",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        450.1639404296875,
        563.0404663085938,
        459.9258728027344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the normalized position, sine/cosine of the orientation, and",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        462.1593322753906,
        563.0353393554688,
        471.0658874511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the normalized range and sine/cosine of the bearing to each",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        473.9953308105469,
        563.035400390625,
        482.9018859863281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obstacle. Each network was trained for 5 million timesteps.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        485.830322265625,
        556.0514526367188,
        494.73687744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Across 100 trials with differing initial states, we compared",
      "bbox": [
        321.93988037109375,
        497.66632080078125,
        563.0347290039062,
        506.5728759765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the actor policy against AC-PAC-NMPC for each γc. We eval-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778747558594,
        509.3429260253906,
        563.036376953125,
        519.1038818359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uated the percentage of trials in which the system collided with",
      "bbox": [
        311.97784423828125,
        521.3372802734375,
        563.0352172851562,
        530.2438354492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obstacles and reached the goal without colliding. Additionally,",
      "bbox": [
        311.97784423828125,
        533.17333984375,
        563.0352783203125,
        542.0798950195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "we evaluated our RL-based warm-start with and without the",
      "bbox": [
        311.97784423828125,
        545.00927734375,
        563.0353393554688,
        553.9158325195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "actor infeasibility check (lines 6-8 in Algo. 1).",
      "bbox": [
        311.97784423828125,
        556.8442993164062,
        503.5086364746094,
        565.7508544921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "As shown in Figure 18, AC-PAC-NMPC was able to",
      "bbox": [
        321.9398498535156,
        568.6802978515625,
        563.0347290039062,
        577.5868530273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "successfully navigate the environment at smaller γc values",
      "bbox": [
        311.97784423828125,
        580.3568725585938,
        563.0361938476562,
        590.9168701171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "than the actor policy alone. This supports Theorem VIII.2",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        592.351318359375,
        563.0354614257812,
        601.2578735351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "empirically and shows that for a large enough penalty, a",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        604.1873168945312,
        563.0353393554688,
        613.0938720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "feasible policy exists in the neighborhood of the actor policy",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        616.0233154296875,
        563.0352783203125,
        624.9298706054688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which descends the value function. Additionally, these results",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        627.8583374023438,
        563.03515625,
        636.764892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "show that by warm-starting with the prior policy when the",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        639.6943359375,
        563.0352172851562,
        648.6008911132812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "actor trajectory is infeasible, the safety of AC-PAC-NMPC",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        651.5303344726562,
        563.0353393554688,
        660.4368896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "can be significantly improved.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        663.3652954101562,
        435.3147277832031,
        672.2718505859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "IX. CONCLUSION",
      "bbox": [
        399.2108154296875,
        688.6473388671875,
        475.80743408203125,
        697.5538940429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this paper, we present an approach for RL-guided SN-",
      "bbox": [
        321.9398193359375,
        703.621337890625,
        563.0347900390625,
        712.5278930664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MPC to enable long-range navigation in unknown environ-",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        715.4573364257812,
        563.0353393554688,
        724.3638916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ments while enforcing constraints on probabilistic guarantees",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        727.2922973632812,
        563.0352783203125,
        736.1988525390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of safety. The proposed approach utilized learned actor-critic",
      "bbox": [
        311.9778137207031,
        739.1282958984375,
        563.0352783203125,
        748.0348510742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
  ],
